Node ID=49 the one who owed nobody
Text=It shows. Everyone who has ever come down that passage arrived belonging to something, and the belonging is the first thing I see; it sits on a man like a coat. You came in wearing nothing, which is rarer than you know and worth less than you hope. A coin that refuses to be flipped is still a coin, coinspinner, and the hand will come for it anyway.
